<title>MEXICO: Mexico's preliminary Sept trade surplus $601 mln.</title>
<headline>Mexico's preliminary Sept trade surplus $601 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's preliminary trade surplus in September was $601 million, the result of record exports of $8.376 billion and imports of $7.775 billion, the Finance Ministry said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The surplus was well above the $374 million forecast in a Reuters survey of 11 Mexico City brokerages, and was a strong rebound from the revised August trade surplus of $353 million.</p>
